\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.1}{\ignorespaces The LAS adaptor data flow. The statement $Y$ is folded into the challenge hash during PreSign and PreVerify; the witness $y$ is added by Adapt to turn the pre-signature into an ordinary signature; and publishing that signature lets anyone holding the pre-signature run Extract to recover $y$. This last step is what makes an atomic swap atomic.}}{16}{figure.2.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:flow}{{2.1}{16}{The LAS adaptor data flow. The statement $Y$ is folded into the challenge hash during PreSign and PreVerify; the witness $y$ is added by Adapt to turn the pre-signature into an ordinary signature; and publishing that signature lets anyone holding the pre-signature run Extract to recover $y$. This last step is what makes an atomic swap atomic}{figure.2.1}{}}
\newlabel{fig:flow@cref}{{[figure][1][2]2.1}{[1][16][]16}}
